    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but i've been reading a lot of stuff online lately and honestly it feels like the single-family neighborhood arguments are just excuses to keep people out and keep prices high. like, is there actually any \"science\" or \"data\" behind the idea that density ruins community character, or is that just a way to block progress?",
